            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can a mini split heat a house in winter?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                A cold-climate rated model can, and increasingly does. The specification to check is the temperature at which the unit still delivers 100 percent of rated heating capacity — the best systems hold full output at 5 degrees F and keep producing usable heat to around -13 degrees F. Budget units derate sharply below freezing and should be treated as supplemental heat in northern climates.
              </p>
