                Only a DIY-specific system with a pre-charged quick-connect line set, such as the MRCOOL DIY series. Conventional mini splits require pulling a vacuum on the refrigerant lines and handling refrigerant, which legally requires EPA Section 608 certification. You will still want a licensed electrician for the dedicated 240V circuit, and most jurisdictions require a permit either way.
              </p>
