            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Are mini splits cheaper to run than central air?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Usually yes, for two reasons. Inverter compressors modulate instead of cycling at full power, and ductless delivery avoids the 20 to 30 percent of conditioned air that typical duct systems lose to leakage and to unconditioned attics and crawlspaces. The exception is a multi-zone system running a single small zone, where part-load efficiency is poor.
              </p>
